{"base_rate":0.5050651230101303,"brier":0.37586685962373373,"bss":-0.5036217429916721,"bss_hi":-0.36741576051773567,"bss_lo":-0.6882518817272414,"chart":{"base":[716.9,107.5],"fp":[154.0,192.7],"lead":"62,281.8 272,275.9 482,272 692,267.2","note":{"base":"skill -0.50 — higher than 3% of cities","fp":"low end -4pp, high end +40pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.8 °C — better than 94% of cities","rel":"promised 48% → rained 25%; promised 100% → rained 62%"},"rel":"362.3,358 640.4,299.6 691.1,197"},"country":"WS","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.37808972503617944,"ess":373.30686803587344,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Apia</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Apia rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>62%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(29%), there is still roughly a <b>12%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 691 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 4.1 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.50, ranked 206 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(203&ndash;209) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'><b>12%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>68%</td><td class='num'><b>40%</b></td><td class='num'>63</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>89%</td><td class='num'><b>39%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>95%</td><td class='num'><b>38%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>62%</b></td><td class='num'>424</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Apia</b> <span class=\"muted\">Samoa</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>-0.50</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>203&ndash;209\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>691 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Apia &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Apia\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"159.63391304347826,239.56521739130434 300.2933333333334,93.11111111111114 371.5642253521127,33.38028169014086 395.6828125,18.0 411.4907075471698,18.0 411.4907075471698,20.575471698113176 395.6828125,52.125 371.5642253521127,84.64788732394368 300.2933333333334,174.0 159.63391304347826,313.4202898550725\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"198.15629522431257\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"198.15629522431257\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"159.63391304347826,339.7971014492754 300.2933333333334,237.55555555555557 371.5642253521127,238.45070422535213 395.6828125,245.5 411.4907075471698,155.35849056603774\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 29%&amp;#10;It rained 12% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"159.63391304347826\" cy=\"339.7971014492754\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 68%&amp;#10;It rained 40% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 63 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"300.2933333333334\" cy=\"237.55555555555557\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 89%&amp;#10;It rained 39% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"371.5642253521127\" cy=\"238.45070422535213\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 95%&amp;#10;It rained 38% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"395.6828125\" cy=\"245.5\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 62% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 424 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.4907075471698\" cy=\"155.35849056603774\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(51%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Apia the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.11) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-1.23).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>170</td><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'>-1.233</td><td class='num'>50.1%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>173</td><td class='num'>49%</td><td class='num'>-0.630</td><td class='num'>41.6%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>185</td><td class='num'>52%</td><td class='num'>-0.521</td><td class='num'>36.3%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>163</td><td class='num'>71%</td><td class='num'>-0.112</td><td class='num'>22.7%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":-13.83333,"lon":-171.76666,"n":691,"n_cities":213,"name":"Apia","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.51,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.2871014492753623,"n":69,"obs":0.11594202898550725,"sig":true},{"hi":0.82,"lo":0.51,"mean":0.6844444444444446,"n":63,"obs":0.3968253968253968,"sig":true},{"hi":0.94,"lo":0.82,"mean":0.8857746478873241,"n":71,"obs":0.39436619718309857,"sig":true},{"hi":0.98,"lo":0.94,"mean":0.95390625,"n":64,"obs":0.375,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.98,"mean":0.9985613207547169,"n":424,"obs":0.6226415094339622,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":4.1,"provisional":false,"rank":206,"rank_hi":209.0,"rank_lo":203.0,"reliability":0.15303129671558013,"resolution":0.02749646198795415,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"apia","station":"","timezone":"Pacific/Apia"}